// §4.5.15, third bullet, verbatim: "Analog operators are not allowed in the
// repeat, while and non-genvar for looping statements." §5.9 states the same
// restriction from the statement side: "The following restrictions are applied
// to looping statements (repeat, while and for) except for analog_for
// statements: - Analog filter functions are not allowed".
//
// Neither clause carries an analysis_or_constant carve-out: §4.5.15 grants one
// to `if`/`case`/`?:` in its FIRST bullet only, and a repeat count that cannot
// change during the simulation still does not license a filter in the body.
// (The event-body ban is a third, separate bullet — 88_operator_in_event.va.)
//
// This fixture used to assert the opposite — that the illegal form COMPILES.
//! lrm 4.5.15
//! reject E0514
// §5.9: "Analog filter functions are not allowed" in repeat/while/non-genvar
// for. The `analog_for` (genvar) form IS allowed, because it unrolls onto the
// spine — see 92_operator_in_genvar_for.va. Rejected as E0514.
module ch4_op_repeat(p); inout p; electrical p; real x; analog begin repeat(2) x=ddt(V(p)); I(p)<+x; end endmodule
